.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH elfshaker-esi 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-esi \- Creates and edits elfshaker remote indexes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker esi\fR [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates and edits elfshaker remote indexes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
elfshaker\-esi\-create(1)
Creates an empty ESI index
.TP
elfshaker\-esi\-list(1)
Lists entries in an ESI index
.TP
elfshaker\-esi\-add(1)
Adds packs to one or more ESI indexes
.TP
elfshaker\-esi\-remove(1)
Removes pack URLs from one or more ESI indexes
